Passing the already acquired physical variance into the count domain
==================================================================

For the same actual standardized marginal, let p=P(X>0), q=1-p, v=pq,
m=E X_+=E X_->0, and ell=m/v. In the sign-conditioned count decomposition
X=ell(B+U-p), E(U|B)=0 and s=q E(U0²)+p E(U1²). Variance1 gives
ell²(v+s)=1. The physical within-sign variance theta equals ell²s. Hence

       theta=s/(v+s),       lambda=n*s=n*v*theta/(1-theta).

If an independently acquired same-law bound gives theta<=T<1, then
lambda<=n*vmax*T/(1-T), where vmax is the exact maximum of p(1-p) on
the count's closed probability interval. This maximum is1/4 if the interval
contains1/2, and otherwise the larger endpoint value. The expression is
increasing in v>0 and theta in[0,1), so this upper bound is rigorous on both
probability halves and at theta=0. All operations are rational.

Intersect only the current lambda coordinate interval with this new bound.
An empty intersection requires a strict incoming lower>new upper; equality
is retained. No bound or coordinate of the original root box is omitted:
the finite-tree acceptor must reconstruct that root and rerun this necessary
contraction at every leaf.

IMPORTANT: the pre-existing contract field Lambda is also the intercept of
coupled moment/gap inequalities, such as d<=d0(1-lambda/Lambda). It cannot
be replaced by the new smaller scalar cap. Every original price, d0,
quadratic, Lambda and coupled plane is retained unchanged. The new contract
field acquired_theta_upper is a separate physical premise, requiring a
fresh exact same-law resource interface. No stronger joint inequality is
asserted. An exact resource's raw_row.theta is the relevant physical bound;
it is not itself lambda or lambda/n.

The independent source derivation and finite-law checks are in
new_audit/THETA_LAMBDA_INDEPENDENT_DERIVATION.txt and THETA_LAMBDA_CHECKED.json.
This lemma is only a conditional domain contraction. It does not establish
resource acquisition, any entire count forest, or the cutoff25 by itself.
